  "body": "This seems a bit weird. Limiting to the install event seems like is meant to prevent old versions of a SW from getting events only the new version cares about, but because subscriptions are stored on the registration (as opposed to the actual worker), the old version will still get events the new version subscribed for, until that new version becomes the active version.\r\n\r\nPerhaps two possible more sensible ways would to either:\r\n\r\n1. Change subscription to be on ServiceWorkerRegistration, like push API (and allow changes at any time). That at least makes it clear that it is a per registration thing.\r\n\r\n2. Or change subscriptions to be per service worker version rather than registration, and perhaps change the API to be exposed on InstallEvent rather than the cookie store object?",
